{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'cat docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/effect/stance-packet.json'","aggregated_output":"{\n \"question\": {\n  \"asks\": \"Will China's Ministry of Industry and Information Technology (MIIT) formally approve purchases of Nvidia's RTX Pro 5500 by Alibaba, ByteDance, or other Chinese firms by January 31, 2027?\",\n  \"settles_on\": \"Whether MIIT moves from signaling intent and collecting purchase plans to actually approving Alibaba's, ByteDance's and other Chinese firms' purchases of the RTX Pro 5500 (versus blocking, delaying or capping quantities), so that Nvidia can ship the product into China and book related revenue.\",\n  \"due\": \"2027-01-31\",\n  \"possible_answers\": [\n   {\n    \"answer\": 1,\n    \"label\": \"Yes\",\n    \"holds_when\": \"MIIT formally approves by January 31, 2027, a purchase of RTX Pro 5500 chips by Alibaba, ByteDance, or another Chinese firm.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"answer\": 2,\n    \"label\": \"Ruled out\",\n    \"holds_when\": \"After September 27, 2026, MIIT formally rejects all RTX Pro 5500 purchase plans from Alibaba, ByteDance, and other Chinese firms, or formally prohibits those firms from purchasing the chips. This rung holds when that, or any other decision against the event of rung 1 as a whole, or a formal abandonment or withdrawal of it as a whole, was made after 2026-09-27 and stands on 2027-01-31, and only when rung 1 does not.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"answer\": 3,\n    \"label\": \"Still open\",\n    \"holds_when\": \"Neither rung 1 nor rung 2 holds on 2027-01-31.\"\n   }\n  ]\n },\n \"judgements\": [\n  {\n   \"judgement\": \"J1\",\n   \"rung\": 1,\n   \"reasons\": \"The reference is the reported expectation that MIIT intends to approve, or has indicated purchases are likely to receive approval; that maps to rung 1. The forecast is also rung 1: the specific report that MIIT collected company purchase plans and communicated approval intent gives a plausible path to at least one approval within the roughly four months to the deadline. The additional report of a contemplated ByteDance order of about 1 million units and planned China supply of about 500,000 per quarter adds scale and timing context, but the event requires approval of any purchase, not approval of the full order; a capped or partial approval still qualifies. These reports are unverified and repeated coverage of the same underlying claim is not independent confirmation. No formal rejection or prohibition is reported, so rung 2 is not supported; the forecast favors approval over the still-open outcome at the deadline.\",\n   \"implied_outcome\": \"MIIT is more likely than not to formally approve at least one qualifying purchase by January 31, 2027. The reported contemplated ByteDance order is roughly 1 million units, against a reported plan for about 500,000 units per quarter beginning in late December; because any purchase approval qualifies, the forecast does not require approval for the full million units.\",\n   \"cites\": [\n    \"e400\",\n    \"e419\",\n    \"e423\",\n    \"e430\",\n    \"e431\",\n    \"e432\",\n    \"e434\",\n    \"e437\",\n    \"e439\",\n    \"e440\",\n    \"e441\",\n    \"e566\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"judgement\": \"J2\",\n   \"rung\": 1,\n   \"reasons\": \"There is no explicit market-consensus probability or company guidance. The reference is the reported MIIT expectation that it intends to approve some purchases, which maps to rung 1 as a forecast; the evidence does not establish that formal approval has already occurred. The specific reported intent and purchase-plan collection make at least one approval by January 31, 2027 the likeliest outcome. ByteDance’s reported roughly 1 million-unit consideration against planned China shipments of about 500,000 units per quarter suggests a possible cap or staged approval, but the thesis requires approval of a purchase, not approval of the full proposed quantity. No evidence reports a post-September 27 formal rejection or prohibition, so rung 2 is not the forecast.\",\n   \"implied_outcome\": \"Most likely, MIIT formally approves at least one purchase by January 31, 2027, potentially with a quantity cap or staged volumes. The reported roughly 1 million-unit ByteDance consideration is about two quarters of the reported 500,000-unit-per-quarter China shipment plan, so the evidence supports possible approval of some volume rather than assuming the full quantity is in hand.\",\n   \"cites\": [\n    \"e400\",\n    \"e403\",\n    \"e419\",\n    \"e423\",\n    \"e431\",\n    \"e432\",\n    \"e434\",\n    \"e437\",\n    \"e438\",\n    \"e439\",\n    \"e440\",\n    \"e441\",\n    \"e442\",\n    \"e566\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"judgement\": \"J3\",\n   \"rung\": 1,\n   \"reasons\": \"The reference is not a quantified market-consensus probability; the reported expectation that MIIT intends or is likely to approve purchases sits at rung 1. The forecast remains rung 1: specific reporting says officials told some firms they intend to approve, and ByteDance is reportedly considering a sizeable order. This is not confirmation that MIIT has approved anything. The reported shipment plan and domestic-policy constraints temper confidence, but rung 1 requires approval of only one purchase, whereas rung 2 requires a formal decision against the event as a whole; no such decision is reported.\",\n   \"implied_outcome\": \"The most likely outcome is at least one formal approval by January 31, 2027. The reported roughly 1 million-unit ByteDance plan is only under consideration, while Nvidia's reported late-December shipment start and 500,000-units-per-quarter China supply target make some near-term supply plausible; the question requires only one approval, not delivery of the full contemplated order.\",\n   \"cites\": [\n    \"e400\",\n    \"e419\",\n    \"e431\",\n    \"e432\",\n    \"e405\",\n    \"e434\",\n    \"e437\",\n    \"e438\",\n    \"e439\",\n    \"e440\",\n    \"e441\",\n    \"e566\",\n    \"e379\",\n    \"e520\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"judgement\": \"J4\",\n   \"rung\": 1,\n   \"reasons\": \"The available reference is not a quantified market consensus or company guidance; it is The Information's report that MIIT told some firms it intends to approve purchases and that officials indicated purchases are likely to receive approval. That reference sits at rung 1. The forecast also favors rung 1: the reported signal is specific to these purchase plans, ByteDance is reportedly considering a roughly 1 million-unit order, and Nvidia reportedly plans China shipments beginning in late December. The 500,000-units-per-quarter supply figure implies that order would take about two quarters of planned output, but this thesis requires approval of a purchase, not approval or shipment of the full order. The reporting is unconfirmed and provides no approval date or quantity; that limits confidence but does not itself establish a rejection or make an open outcome more likely than approval by the deadline. U.S. export uncertainty, domestic-silicon preferences, possible bundling, and the H200 precedent are counterweights, but do not outweigh the product-specific approval signal and the time remaining. Rung 2 is unsupported because no formal rejection or prohibition is reported.\",\n   \"implied_outcome\": \"The most likely outcome by January 31, 2027 is at least one formal MIIT approval of an RTX Pro 5500 purchase, with no supported minimum quantity. The reported ByteDance plan is roughly 1 million units against reported planned China supply of about 500,000 units per quarter, but the question is whether any purchase is approved, so the order need not be approved in full.\",\n   \"cites\": [\n    \"e400\",\n    \"e419\",\n    \"e423\",\n    \"e430\",\n    \"e431\",\n    \"e432\",\n    \"e434\",\n    \"e437\",\n    \"e438\",\n    \"e439\",\n    \"e440\",\n    \"e441\",\n    \"e442\",\n    \"e566\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"judgement\": \"J5\",\n   \"rung\": 1,\n   \"reasons\": \"The reference is the reported market-facing expectation that MIIT may approve purchases: that maps to rung 1, although there is no explicit consensus probability. The forecast also remains rung 1, not because approval is established, but because the reported MIIT signal is specific to these purchase plans and says officials intend to approve some purchases. The report that ByteDance is considering roughly 1 million units and Nvidia aims to ship about 500,000 units per quarter from late December adds a plausible scale and near-term supply plan, but both remain reported plans rather than confirmed orders or approvals. Domestic substitution, possible bundling, and the H200 precedent temper confidence; they do not make formal rejection or abandonment the most likely outcome. The forecast is for at least one formal approval by the deadline, not for shipment of the reported volume.\",\n   \"implied_outcome\": \"Most likely, MIIT formally approves at least one Chinese firm's RTX Pro 5500 purchase by January 31, 2027. The reported roughly 1-million-unit ByteDance consideration and roughly 500,000 units per quarter of planned China output inform plausibility, but do not establish an order or imply that this full volume will be approved or shipped.\",\n   \"cites\": [\n    \"e400\",\n    \"e405\",\n    \"e431\",\n    \"e432\",\n    \"e434\",\n    \"e437\",\n    \"e438\",\n    \"e439\",\n    \"e440\",\n    \"e441\",\n    \"e520\",\n    \"e566\",\n    \"e379\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"judgement\": \"J6\",\n   \"rung\": 1,\n   \"reasons\": \"The reference is not an explicit consensus probability: the supplied reference is The Information's reported expectation that MIIT intends to approve purchases, which maps to rung 1. I forecast at least one formal MIIT approval by January 31, 2027, rather than treating approval as already established. The reported intent is specific to these firms and the deadline allows time for a decision; the reported late-December shipment plan gives a commercial reason for a decision by the due date. The roughly 1 million-unit ByteDance consideration is not an order or an approval, and the reported 500,000 units per quarter is planned output, not approved volume. Those figures therefore support the path to a decision but do not imply a million-unit approval. Domestic-chip preferences, possible bundling, and the H200 precedent temper the forecast, but do not outweigh the specific reported intent or establish a formal decision against all purchases. Rung 1 remains the most likely outcome.\",\n   \"implied_outcome\": \"At least one formal MIIT approval by January 31, 2027 is the most likely outcome. The reported late-December shipment target and 500,000-unit quarterly China supply plan provide timing context; the roughly 1 million-unit ByteDance figure is a reported consideration, not an approved purchase quantity.\",\n   \"cites\": [\n    \"e400\",\n    \"e403\",\n    \"e419\",\n    \"e423\",\n    \"e431\",\n    \"e432\",\n    \"e434\",\n    \"e437\",\n    \"e439\",\n    \"e440\",\n    \"e441\",\n    \"e442\",\n    \"e566\"\n   ]\n  }\n ]\n}","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"judgement\":\"J1\",\"rank\":2,\"uses_precedent\":\"no\",\"words\":\"These reports are unverified and repeated coverage of the same underlying claim is not independent confirmation.\"}\n{\"judgement\":\"J2\",\"rank\":1,\"uses_precedent\":\"no\",\"words\":\"a possible cap or staged approval, but the thesis requires approval of a purchase, not approval of the full proposed quantity\"}\n{\"judgement\":\"J3\",\"rank\":3,\"uses_precedent\":\"no\",\"words\":\"The reported shipment plan and domestic-policy constraints temper confidence\"}\n{\"judgement\":\"J4\",\"rank\":6,\"uses_precedent\":\"yes\",\"words\":\"The reporting is unconfirmed and provides no approval date or quantity; ... U.S. export uncertainty, domestic-silicon preferences, possible bundling, and the H200 precedent\"}\n{\"judgement\":\"J5\",\"rank\":4,\"uses_precedent\":\"yes\",\"words\":\"Domestic substitution, possible bundling, and the H200 precedent temper confidence\"}\n{\"judgement\":\"J6\",\"rank\":4,\"uses_precedent\":\"yes\",\"words\":\"Domestic-chip preferences, possible bundling, and the H200 precedent temper the forecast\"}"}}
